# Sourced by dhcpcd-run-hooks, before 10-wpa_supplicant (numeric prefix, lexical glob order -
# dhcpcd-run-hooks.in sources every file under @HOOKDIR@/* into itself with ". $hook" in one
# shell, earliest name first, and a variable a hook sets is still there for the next one).
#
# etc/dhcpcd.conf sets "env wpa_supplicant_driver=nl80211,wext" at global scope (X6, 2026-09-26),
# which dhcpcd.conf.5.in documents as reaching the hooks' environment - but on the console
# (dhcpcd 9.4.1, PRIVSEP on, -B --noarp) the running wpa_supplicant never carries the -D that
# 10-wpa_supplicant's "driver=${wpa_supplicant_driver:+-D}$wpa_supplicant_driver" would add, with
# or without that env line (seen 2026-09-26, todo K9 - the "env" config option's value is not
# landing in $wpa_supplicant_driver by the time 10-wpa_supplicant runs; root cause not pinned
# down, could be a PRIVSEP build detail of this dhcpcd or a quirk of Buildroot's own build of it).
#
# Whatever the cause, set the fallback here instead, where sourcing order guarantees it is seen:
# a plain shell default-assign, so a value dhcpcd DID manage to pass through still wins over it.
: "${wpa_supplicant_driver:=nl80211,wext}"
